    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot In detail
      | What each mark means

    h3 What is CE Certification?
    p CE (Conformité Européenne) marking indicates that a product meets the safety, health, and environmental requirements of the European Economic Area. It's a mandatory requirement for products sold in the EU.

    h3 What is UKCA Certification?
    p UKCA (UK Conformity Assessed) marking is the UK's equivalent to CE marking, required for products sold in Great Britain. It ensures products meet UK safety standards.

    h3 What is RoHS?
    p RoHS (Restriction of Hazardous Substances) restricts the use of specific hazardous materials in electrical and electronic equipment — making products safer for users and the environment.

